{#
calendar/_lists.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The response to every calendar mutation: create, rename, recolour, show/hide,
make default, delete, subscribe, unsubscribe, sync now, and connecting a CalDAV
server.

One region today — the settings list. Written as a stream per region anyway,
the way the label version is, because a stream whose target is absent is a
no-op: when a calendar picker appears in the sidebar it becomes another
turbo-stream block here and every existing caller starts refreshing it.

The connectable sources ride along in the same replacement rather than in a
second stream block, because they live inside `settings-calendar-list`:
connecting a CalDAV server has to make its row appear immediately, and a
replacement that redrew only the calendars would leave the new server invisible
until the page was reloaded.

Variables:
  calendars            Calendar[]     in sort order
  calendarAccounts     Account[]      accounts calendars can be subscribed from
  calendarConnections  Integration[]  calendar connections
  toastMessage         string         translation key
  toastParameters      array          placeholders for it, e.g. { '%count%': 2 }
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            message: toastMessage|trans(toastParameters|default({})),
            type: 'success',
        } %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

{# The target id is re-emitted inside its own replacement. A replace whose
   template drops the id works exactly once: the second stream finds nothing
   called settings-calendar-list and silently does nothing. #}
<turbo-stream action="replace" target="settings-calendar-list">
    <template>
        <div id="settings-calendar-list">
            {% include 'settings/_calendars.html.twig' with {
                calendars: calendars,
                calendarAccounts: calendarAccounts|default([]),
                calendarConnections: calendarConnections|default([]),
            } only %}
        </div>
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
